From: Jeff Williams <jeff@wdwconsulting.net>
Date: Thu, 21 Aug 2026 23:10:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: lpc32xx: select GPIO function for GPIO_00..05 on output

The LPC32xx has no pinctrl driver, and pins GPIO_00..GPIO_05 are muxed
with alternate functions (SSEL0/1, etc.) selected via the P2_MUX
register. When the bootloader leaves such a pin in its alternate
function, the gpiolib output writes (P3_OUTP) never reach the pin, so a
consumer driving the line as a GPIO has no effect.

This breaks SPI with a GPIO chip-select: on the SnapAV WattBox the SPI
NOR chip-select is GPIO_05, which resets to the SSEL0 function; the
mainline spi-pl022 gpio-CS then never selects the flash and spi-nor
reads back all-0xff JEDEC id, even though clock, mode and CS direction
are all correct.

Clear the pin's P2_MUX bit when it is requested as an output so the
GPIO function actually drives the pad. This matches what the vendor
bootloader does before bit-banging these lines.

Signed-off-by: Jeff Williams <jeff@wdwconsulting.net>
---
 drivers/gpio/gpio-lpc32xx.c |    9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-lpc32xx.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-lpc32xx.c
@@ -325,6 +325,15 @@ static int lpc32xx_gpio_dir_output_p3(st
 {
 	struct lpc32xx_gpio_chip *group = gpiochip_get_data(chip);
 
+	/*
+	 * GPIO_00..GPIO_05 share pins with alternate functions (SSEL0/1, ...)
+	 * selected via P2_MUX. This SoC has no pinctrl driver, so if the
+	 * bootloader left the pin in its alternate function, GPIO output writes
+	 * never reach the pin (observed: SPI gpio-CS on GPIO_05 muxed as SSEL0
+	 * -> chip never selected -> spi-nor reads 0xff). Force GPIO function.
+	 */
+	gpreg_write(group, (1 << pin), LPC32XX_GPIO_P2_MUX_CLR);
+
 	__set_gpio_level_p3(group, pin, value);
 	__set_gpio_dir_p3(group, pin, 0);
 
